{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "userdb-hotelling-threeyear-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.70, step 7f. PENDING. `userdb-hotelling-threeyear`: `userdb-hotelling-multiyear` at THREE calendar years, 2015, 2020 and 2025 -- the same selections (Total Energy at running exhaust, extended idle and APU; the passenger car and the combination long-haul truck; April and August, both day types, hours 7 and 8; DEFAULT domain) over the same user input database with every year-keyed table stated at 2025 too and `hotellingHoursPerDay` 1900 / 2300 hours at 2025 (`db_hotellinghoursperday` overrides the domain document's). MOVESOutput is 24,288 rows; 2015's and 2020's are `userdb-hotelling-multiyear`'s to the digit.\n\nWHAT IT WAITS ON: AdjustHotelling.sql at a THIRD calendar year (`hot_adjustmentRowsUnported`, read by `run_domainUnported`, counts this run's 89 adjustment rows). TotalActivityGenerator clears hotellingHours only when the process changes, so when it adjusts 2025 the table holds 2015's rows as 2020's hour, age and month blocks left them -- rescaled a second time -- beside 2020's, and 2025's defaults pool all three years and rescale every row. Measured in pandas (PLAN.md §7.3.70): replaying the four blocks over `userdb-hotelling-multiyear`'s final table plus 2025's own TAG hours reproduces all 2952 rows of this run's final hotellingHours, every year's, at 9.5e-15; pooling 2020's rows alone misses 2025 by up to 84% (median 23%), adjusting 2025 alone by up to x2.75. The table each year adjusts over is the previous year's table times that year's three block factors, plus that year's own rows: a recurrence over the year axis whose step normalises a whole slice (each default is a ratio of sums over the other axes), which a §4.3.1.2 recurrence group cannot express -- its reads must be the identity on every axis but the recurrence's. Two years are ported (§7.3.61); the model does not carry N. Evaluated anyway on the two-year chain: 2015's and 2020's rows within 1.2e-05, every 2025 extended-idle and APU cell wrong, by up to 31% (572 cells over tolerance).\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 3036, the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs per (county, month, hour-day) cell over the three years, as the evaluation recomputed it (`rateSurvivorCount`). `n_sourceBin` is 4: at 3, the two-year runs' value, one source bin of a 2025 cohort falls past the last slot (`run_sourceBinsDropped` 1).\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "idle-adjustment",
      "hotelling-adjustment",
      "user-input-database",
      "multi-year"
    ]
  },
